295 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 246 0 R
/T (Climate change is not only increasing health risks in Kenya and South Africa; it is exposing how access to healthcare is organised when systems come under pressure. Across flooded informal settlements, overcrowded clinics, and drought-affected regions, the question is no longer simply whether healthcare exists, but who is able to reach it, enter it, and be recognised within it.)
/E (Climate change is not only increasing health risks in Kenya and South Africa; it is exposing how access to healthcare is organised when systems come under pressure. Across flooded informal settlements, overcrowded clinics, and drought-affected regions, the question is no longer simply whether healthcare exists, but who is able to reach it, enter it, and be recognised within it.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
296 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 246 0 R
/T (Evidence from both countries shows that health systems do not respond to medical need alone. Access is shaped by administrative processes, documentation requirements, and decisions made at the point of service. As floods, droughts, and extreme heat increase demand for healthcare, migrants, refugees, and other mobile populations often encounter systems that were not designed with mobility in )
/E (Evidence from both countries shows that health systems do not respond to medical need alone. Access is shaped by administrative processes, documentation requirements, and decisions made at the point of service. As floods, droughts, and extreme heat increase demand for healthcare, migrants, refugees, and other mobile populations often encounter systems that were not designed with mobility in )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
297 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 246 0 R
/T (mind. The report identifies two distinct governance patterns. In Kenya, access is shaped primarily through administrative recognition. Refugees, asylum seekers, and other displaced populations must be visible within state systems to obtain healthcare, yet fragmented databases, documentation barriers, and parallel humanitarian structures continue to limit this recognition. In South Africa, access is formally guaranteed but unevenly applied. Legal entitlement exists, but healthcare access is frequently shaped by frontline decisions, documentation checks, institutional discretion, and uncertainty over who belongs within an already overburdened system.)
/E (mind. The report identifies two distinct governance patterns. In Kenya, access is shaped primarily through administrative recognition. Refugees, asylum seekers, and other displaced populations must be visible within state systems to obtain healthcare, yet fragmented databases, documentation barriers, and parallel humanitarian structures continue to limit this recognition. In South Africa, access is formally guaranteed but unevenly applied. Legal entitlement exists, but healthcare access is frequently shaped by frontline decisions, documentation checks, institutional discretion, and uncertainty over who belongs within an already overburdened system.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
