/T (The study engaged 62 participants, including refugees, asylum seekers, migrants, healthcare workers, humanitarian actors, community representatives and government officials working across health, migration and environmental sectors. Of these, 32 interviews were conducted in Kenya, focusing on Nairobi and refugee camp settings, while the remaining 30 interviews were conducted in South Africa, focusing on Gauteng and KwaZulu-Natal. Representatives of refugee-led organisations and community health promoters were also included to capture local experiences of healthcare access and service delivery.)
/E (The study engaged 62 participants, including refugees, asylum seekers, migrants, healthcare workers, humanitarian actors, community representatives and government officials working across health, migration and environmental sectors. Of these, 32 interviews were conducted in Kenya, focusing on Nairobi and refugee camp settings, while the remaining 30 interviews were conducted in South Africa, focusing on Gauteng and KwaZulu-Natal. Representatives of refugee-led organisations and community health promoters were also included to capture local experiences of healthcare access and service delivery.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
