<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 249 0 R
/T (Field observations in clinics, informal settlements, and refugee-hosting areas were used to complement interview data, alongside a review of policy documents, health data, and reports on climate-related events in both countries. This allowed the study to connect lived experiences of healthcare access with broader institutional and policy dynamics. All participants provided informed consent prior to participation, and ethical)
/E (Field observations in clinics, informal settlements, and refugee-hosting areas were used to complement interview data, alongside a review of policy documents, health data, and reports on climate-related events in both countries. This allowed the study to connect lived experiences of healthcare access with broader institutional and policy dynamics. All participants provided informed consent prior to participation, and ethical)
/Pg 14 0 R
