<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 258 0 R
/E (Administrative uncertainty deepened these barriers. Persistent backlogs within the Department of Home Affairs left many asylum seekers and migrants in prolonged states of legal limbo, relying on temporary or expired permits. This had direct consequences for healthcare access. Many interviewees described avoiding clinics altogether due to fear of exposure to immigration enforcement or humiliation during registration processes. Others relied on churches, migrant community groups, or informal networks to identify which facilities were safer to approach, what documents to carry, and when to seek care to minimise confrontation.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
