1602 0 obj
<<
/Title (mind. The report identifies two distinct governance patterns. In Kenya, access is shaped primarily through administrative recognition. Refugees, asylum seekers, and other displaced populations must be visible within state systems to obtain healthcare, yet fragmented databases, documentation barriers, and parallel humanitarian structures continue to limit this recognition. In South Africa, access is formally guaranteed but unevenly applied. Legal entitlement exists, but healthcare access is frequently shaped by frontline decisions, documentation checks, institutional discretion, and uncertainty over who belongs within an already overburdened system.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 38 0 R
/Prev 1446 0 R
/Next 1685 0 R
>>
endobj
